  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen capacities to fight the illicit trafficking of cultural property and promote its return and restitution, to protect underwater cultural heritage and to promote the role of museums for societies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support will be provided to Member States under the Santiago Regional Office for the implementation of the 1970 Convention for preventing and combatting the illicit trafficking of cultural property. As well, advocacy efforts will be undertaken to achieve the ratification of the 2001 Convention in Chile and thereby protect the underwater cultural heritage and prevent the pillage of it. More specifically capacity building, awareness-raising, and and policy support activities related to the fight and illicit trafficking and the relevance of underwater cultural heritage.</narrative>
  </description>
